s of length2: \"00\",\"01\",\"10\",\"11\". All valid. So dp[2][00]=1, dp[2][01]=1, dp[2][10]=1, dp[2][11]=1.\n\nNow for n>=3: transition: to append a bit to a string of length n-1, we need to ensure no 3 in a row. So if last two bits are XY, and we append Z, we must avoid X=Y=Z. So if last two bits are 00, we cannot append 0. So from state 00 we can only append 1 leading to new last two bits 01. Similarly from 11 cannot append 1, only 0 leading to 10. From 01 we can append 0 or 1: appending 0 gives last two bits 10; appending 1 gives 11. From 10 similarly: append 0 -> 00; append 1 -> 01.\n\nThus transition matrix:\n\nFrom 00 -> 01\nFrom 01 -> 10, "}}],"created":1790960568,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Ftty1elcWZtakbs6p3c3BeCAc8ODMAZH","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":483.612,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.11763853077110192,"prompt_per_second":8500.61619645501,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2349.238,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0628917861799216,"predicted_per_second":326.48884446786576}}